---
/**
 * Scenario index.
 *
 * A short list of hand-written loads. This is not a generated page farm: each
 * entry below was written to answer one search-shaped question, and each one
 * links to the calculator with the load already filled in.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { scenarios } from '../../data/scenarios.ts';
---

<Base
  title="Sizing scenarios"
  description="Worked portable power station loads: a CPAP night, a fridge outage, a camping day, and a power tool off grid. Each one names the limit that binds first."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-14">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Sizing scenarios</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-lg leading-7 text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Each scenario below is a worked load with the reasoning shown: which devices, how many hours,
      what the daily watt-hours come to, and which limit fails first. Every one of them opens in the
      calculator with the load already filled in, so you can change a number and watch the answer
      move.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[68ch] text-sm text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-400">
      Device wattages come from the library on the calculator page, and most of them are published
      engineering ranges rather than measurements. Treat every figure as a planning estimate.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        scenarios.map((s) => (
          <article class="flex flex-col rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-ink-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-ink-800 dark:bg-ink-900">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
              <a href={`/scenarios/${s.id}/`} class="hover:text-moss-700 dark:hover:text-moss-300">
                {s.title}
              </a>
            </h2>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm font-medium text-moss-700 dark:text-moss-300">{s.question}</p>
            <p class="mt-3 flex-1 text-sm leading-6 text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">{s.lede}</p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-sm">
              <a
                href={`/scenarios/${s.id}/`}
                class="press inline-block min-h-11 rounded-[var(--radius-control)] border border-ink-200 px-3 py-2 font-medium hover:border-moss-500 dark:border-ink-700"
              >
                See the worked load
              </a>
            </p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 max-w-[68ch] text-sm text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      These are the loads people ask about most often, not a generated list. If your load is not here,
      the
      <a href="/calculator/" class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300">calculator</a>
      takes any combination, and the
      <a href="/methodology/" class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300">methodology</a>
      page records the formulas and constants behind the numbers.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
